## What was wrong

Both symptoms came from a single rule in `style.css`:

```css
.modules-center {
    padding-right: 24px;
}
```

The base pill padding is `padding: 4px 12px` (12px left, 12px right). This override bumped the center pill to **12px left / 36px right** — that's your uneven left/right padding.

And because the workspace numbers are the rightmost content when no apps are open, that same extra 24px pushed the numbers inward — which is why "the numbers are equally padded to the side" with nothing running.

## The fix

Removed the `padding-right: 24px` override entirely. All three pills (`left`, `center`, `right`) now share the symmetric `4px 12px` padding, so left and right are even and the workspace numbers sit at their natural inset.

